===Verb===
{{en-verb}}
# {{lb|en|rare|historical|transitive}} To pay the [[#Noun|heriot]] on (a piece of [[real estate]]) after the [[death]] of the previous [[tenant]] (such as one's parent, uncle, aunt, or grandparent).
#* {{quote-book |en |year=1904 |title=Halifax Wills: Being Abstracts and Translations of the Wills Registered at York from the Parish of Halifax |volume=2 |url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Halifax_Wills/7atCAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0&bsq=%22herioted%22 |doi= |passage=Page 174, line 25. Perhaps the Richard Longebothome here mentioned was the same man as the Richard who '''herioted''' the property in 1509. Apr. 23, I Hen. VIII (1509). Ric. Longebothome paid xxiijˢ iiijᵈ [23s 4d] fine for license of '''herioting''' one messuage called Longebothome, one cottage, and 40 acres of land and meadow in Soureby after the death of Ric. Longebothome and Agnes, his wife, grandfather {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book |en |year=1909 |editor=William Brown |chapter=Appendix II: Rishworth of Coley |title=Record Series |volume=39: For the Year 1907: Yorkshire Deeds |publisher={{w|Yorkshire Archaeological Society}} |page=226 |url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Record_Series/vPtLAQAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22a%20royd%22&pg=PA227-IA33&printsec=frontcover |doi= |passage=1417. Henry Rishworth formerly held two oxgangs in Hipperholme, Osbarn rode, lands in Coley, etc. His nephew Henry, son of Nicholas de Rishworth, next heir, paid 10s heriot.<br/>1418. John, son and heir of Henry de Rishworth, '''herioted''' a cottage and a royd in the Hey in Hipperholme.}}
#* {{quote-book |en |year=1914 |title=Record Series |volumes=1-3 |publisher=Halifax Antiquarian Society |pages= |isbn= |url= |doi= |passage={{...}} children of his daughter, Agnes Clay, were each to have a cow as their legacies. The will was proved 13th December, 1471. (See Halifax Wills, p. 15.) On the death of his father, William, the wealthy "draper," his  son John '''herioted''' a close called The Holme, with a fulling mill {{...}}}}

